  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe deadline for filing the annual income tax return of an individual taxpayer in the Philippines is on or before the fifteenth (15th) day of April of each year, covering income for the preceding taxable year.\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThis is established under Section 51(C)(1) of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC).\n\n### Interpretation\nSection 51(C)(1) of the NIRC specifies that individual taxpayers must file their income tax returns by April 15 each year. This requirement applies to all individuals subject to income tax, ensuring compliance with the tax obligations for the previous year’s income.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor individual taxpayers, this means that they must prepare and submit their income tax returns by the specified date to avoid penalties and interest for late filing. It is crucial for taxpayers to keep track of this deadline to ensure timely compliance with tax regulations.",
